/* book Worked example: Q: A car covers 1000 km and its owner tops up 0.4 litre of engine oil. Fuel average is 15 km per litre. Find the fuel used, the oil consumption as a fraction of fuel, and the same value as a percentage.
   1. Fuel used Vfuel = D ÷ FE = 1000 km ÷ 15 km/L = 66.7 L.
   2. Oil fraction f = Voil ÷ Vfuel = 0.4 L ÷ 66.7 L = 0.006.
   3. Percentage = f × 100 = 0.006 × 100 = 0.6 percent.
   Answer: Fuel used is 66.7 L; oil consumption is 0.006 of fuel, that is 0.6 percent. */
