/* book exam traps: Blow-by is gas leaking past the piston rings into the crankcase. It is not an exhaust leak and not a valve leak. | The PCV valve passes least at idle, when vacuum is highest, and opens most at full load. Writing it the other way round loses the marks. | A road draft tube is an open system that vents to the air. PCV is a closed system that burns the blow-by in the cylinders. | Do not swap the faults: a valve stuck open gives a lean, rough idle; a valve stuck shut gives crankcase pressure, oil leaks and sludge. | In a turbo engine under boost, blow-by goes to the compressor inlet, not to the pressurised intake manifold. */
